{"id":1840998,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-23T22:53:12.799Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":18,"name":"Drama"}],"homepage":"","id":1840998,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["KR"],"original_language":"ko","original_title":"내 딸아 울지마라","overview":"Sumi works as a bar hostess to raise her only daughter, Jeong-hui. When Jeong-hui collapses with pneumonia, Sumi sells her body to Dal-ho to pay for the surgery. Years later, a grown-up Jeong-hui tells Sumi that she is getting married to Mu-seok. Realizing that Mu-seok is Dal-ho's son, Sumi quietly leaves for the sake of her daughter's happiness. After giving birth to a son, Hun, Jeong-hui enjoys a happy domestic life until she runs into Sumi while out with her in-laws. Once her in-laws uncover the truth about Sumi's past, they kick Jeong-hui out of the house. Despite the help of her brother-in-law, Sang-seok, the cast-out Jeong-hui wanders aimlessly before eventually ending up working as a bar hostess herself. Later, young Hun tracks Jeong-hui down, and a traffic accident involving Sang-seok finally brings an end to the in-laws' resentment. However, in a desperate attempt to pay for Jeong-hui's medical surgery, Sumi steals money and is arrested by the police.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/cMbos30BRRtH2IFfhKAFgGonDey.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":321113,"logo_path":null,"name":"Saehan Film Co., Ltd.","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"KR","name":"South Korea"}],"release_date":"1972-06-17","revenue":0,"runtime":94,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Korean","iso_639_1":"ko","name":"한국어/조선말"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Don't Cry, My Daughter","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":1,"id":1076617,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Kim Ji-mi","original_name":"김지미","popularity":0.4577,"profile_path":"/vBPyW3DICoE